# Golden re-pin ratchet baseline (ADR-0007, production-hardening WS2).
# Commits at or before this SHA are grandfathered: either pre-guard history, or
# reviewed post-guard commits advanced past by this file's documented procedure.
#
# The guard was introduced at dae32d79; bee03042 is the commit it landed on top of.
# The guard is now precise (ADR-0136): it reads the reference run's inputs
# (packages/cross-process-test/src/run-child.ts + verify-golden-hashes.cjs +
# golden/hashes.json) and exempts authored content and the reference-inert
# dock-record plumbing, so deff5d30's no-output changes need neither a trailer
# nor a baseline move.
#
# The shipbuilding-process sprint (INC-1..INC-16; commits afacb248..d4f23d2f)
# changed authoritative package source (phase-engine/commands/ship-design/
# campaign/campaign-engine) with NO golden movement: `pnpm check:golden` verified
# all 10 reference hashes unchanged and `pnpm check:determinism` two runs
# byte-identical throughout. Those commits should each have carried a
# `Golden-Repin: not-needed` trailer; the earlier ones were already pushed by a
# concurrent writer (force-push prohibited) and the later local ones cannot be
# reworded without an interactive rebase (prohibited), so the ratchet baseline is
# advanced past the whole sprint instead, with the reason recorded. The guard
# still applies to every later commit.
#
